   1429  fb08							; ==============================================================================
   1430  fb08							; Bank3-side tramp images (byte-identical with bank2's fetch slots) and
   1431  fb08							; return tails. The `sta $1FF8` at each tail executes bank3-side; the
   1432  fb08							; `jmp` operand bytes at +3 are fetched from bank2 post-switch — bank2's
   1433  fb08							; $FCC1 pads hold the same jmp images.
   1434  fb08							; ==============================================================================
   1435  fb08							; ==============================================================================
   1436  fb08							; A3 (2026-10-19): the pre-read/return tramp images are gone — PhaseBlink,
   1437  fb08							; VcrShutter, HotOverlapBody and the HOV feature dispatcher all live in
   1438  fb08							; bank3 now, so those paths are plain local jmps. What remains here are the
   1439  fb08							; two ENTRY images fetched after a bank0/bank1 `sta $1FF9`.
   1440  fb08							; ==============================================================================
   1441  fb08		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FBEE - *, 0	; VCS3 return pad (twin of bank2 Bank2ReturnPad)
   1442  fbee		       8d f8 1f 	      sta	$1FF8	; $FBEE — sta executes bank3-side
   1443  fbf1		       60		      rts		; $FBF1 — fetched bank2-side post-switch
   1444  fbf2		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FBF8 - *, 0	; B3StageBand/BuildColupF exit: jmp ReturnPad.
   1445  fbf8				   ReturnPad		;   The `sta $1FF6` runs HERE, the `rts` opcode
   1446  fbf8		       8d f6 1f 	      sta	$1FF6	;   is fetched from bank0 at $FBF9 -> pops the
   1447  fbfb		       60		      rts		;   bank0 VBL/jsr caller.
   1448  fbfc		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FC3B - *, 0	; CallPad_BuildColupF entry image: bank0/bank1
   1449  fc3b		       4c c3 f5 	      jmp	BuildColupF	;   execute `sta $1FF9`, this fetch is bank3-side
   1450  fc3e
   1451  fc3e							; VCS3 — OvShutScan body (Phase C kill test; bank2 tramp `sta $1FF9 / jmp
   1452  fc3e							; $FD80` at $FE48). IN: A = kill clock (EnemyRamP-1), Y = MetaB b6 hot bit
   1453  fc3e							; ($40/0 — staged bank2-side; MetaB lives in bank2 models_data ROM, a
   1454  fc3e							; (RoomPF0Lo),Y fetch here would see bank3's pad). OUT (2026-10-14b):
   1455  fc3e							; C=0 passable (A ignored) / C=1 + A≠0 kill / C=1 + A=0 SOLID block —
   1456  fc3e							; returned through the $FBEE pad (sta $1FF8 executed here, rts fetched
   1457  fc3e							; from bank2's byte-identical copy) to OvShutBand's jsr — A and C
   1458  fc3e							; survive both; X/Y clobbered (OvShutBand reloads A before the latch).
   1459  fc3e							; Kill semantics (user spec 2026-10-14, superseded the 2026-10-13
   1460  fc3e							; endpoint-only rule): a horizontal containment gate (after the clock
   1461  fc3e							; math, before the hot/cold split) — the player's lit span must sit
   1462  fc3e							; inside the column [BallX-7, BallX] or the call returns passable
   1463  fc3e							; (side brush, user bug 2026-10-14: touching the closed block from the
   1464  fc3e							; side is not a crunch). Then hot band (MetaB b6) = touching ANY
   1465  fc3e							; closed slice kills (endpoint test ≡ any-part: the ping-pong states
   1466  fc3e							; $11/$1B/$1F never have a closed middle with open ends). Cold band =
   1467  fc3e							; containment only: kill iff the whole sprite sits inside CLOSED
   1468  fc3e							; slices (crunched) — $1F trivially; $1B/$11 iff the box misses the
   1469  fc3e							; aperture (H≥gapHi or F<gapLo). Touching an edge from the open side
   1470  fc3e							; is not a cold kill — that is what the hot flag is for. Every
   1471  fc3e							; NON-kill outcome (side brush, opening half, totally closed, the
   1472  fc3e							; aperture at the player's Y) goes through the solidity test
   1473  fc3e							; (.V3solidBody): both endpoints open → passable, else SOLID block —
   1474  fc3e							; the punched cell must not be walkable through a closed shutter
   1475  fc3e							; (user 2026-10-14b).
   1476  fc3e							; Clock parity: RefreshEnemyY inc'd EnemyRamP at overscan entry, so
   1477  fc3e							; clock-1 = the exact value the kernel rendered slices from this frame.
   1478  fc3e							; Endpoints: RoomY (head) + RoomY+11 (feet = PLAYER_SPRITE_H-1) — every
   1479  fc3e							; open state's gap is >=13 lines ($1B = the 13-line center slice), so
   1480  fc3e							; both endpoints open ⟺ the whole sprite is clear of that state.
   1481  fc3e							; Ping-pong constants (#32/#4) = bank2 VcrCoveredState + CrunchClock
